---
title: "Free Tool to Remove Personal Data From Text"
description: "Paste text and hide names, emails, phone numbers, addresses and card numbers. A local AI model runs in your browser. Nothing is uploaded."
faq:
  - q: "Is the Text Redactor free?"
    a: "Yes. The tool is free, with no account, no sign-up and no limit on how often you use it."
  - q: "Is my text uploaded to a server?"
    a: "No. The page has no server code. Detection runs in your browser, and your text never leaves your device. The only download is the AI model itself, which contains no user data."
  - q: "Does it work offline?"
    a: "After the AI model downloads once, your browser keeps it in its cache. The tool can then detect personal data without a network connection."
  - q: "Which languages does it support?"
    a: "The pattern detectors for emails, phone numbers, cards and IDs work in any language. The AI model that finds names, organizations and places is available for English, Spanish, French, German, Dutch, Chinese, Japanese and Thai."
  - q: "Can someone undo the redaction?"
    a: "No. The tool replaces the original words with labels or blocks in the copied or downloaded text. The original values are not hidden underneath, so there is nothing to recover."
  - q: "Is automatic redaction 100% accurate?"
    a: "No automatic tool is perfect. It can miss unusual names or hide words that are not personal. Always read the result before you share it, click a redaction to keep the original, and add any missed words to the always-hide list."
  - q: "Can I use it to anonymize text before I paste it into ChatGPT or another AI chatbot?"
    a: "Yes. Choose numbered labels such as [NAME_1] and [NAME_2]. Each person keeps the same label all through the text, so the chatbot can still follow who is who without seeing real names."
  - q: "Can I redact PDFs, screenshots or chat logs?"
    a: "This tool is for plain text. For other files, use the PDF Redactor, the Screenshot Redactor or the Chat Text Anonymizer, which run in your browser in the same way."
---

